{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Or a consulter of ov and a knower</b> etc. The Sages taught: a ba'al ov is one who speaks from between the joints and from between the joints of his hands. Rashi explained: he raises the dead person, who sits in one of the joints of the sorcerer's bones, for example on the joints of his fingers or the joints of his knees. The Sages taught: a ba'al ov — this includes both one who raises in his zakhro and one who raises with a skull. 'In his zakhro' — Rashi explained: he raises the dead person upon his male organ; 'with a skull' — the skull detached from the corpse, lying on the ground, and it answers whatever they ask it by means of sorcery. Thus it is taught, and thus Rashi explained in the chapter 'Four Deaths.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "זכרותו is translated literally per Rashi's explanation; the term refers to the male organ."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:18.098191163Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}